$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of 8.4 mmol of amines 3a-3g and
triethyl orthoformate (2) (8.7 mmol, 1.3 g) in 15 mL of dry toluene was
heated under simultaneous distillation by the use of a Dean-Stark trap.
After completion of the reaction, ∼6 h (TLC), the product mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure to its half. A solution of (18.0
mmol, 2.5 g) diethyl hydrogen phosphite (1) in 15 mL of dry toluene
containing sodium metal (18.5 mmol, 0.4 g) was added to the produced
residue dropwise at 0 °C. After warming the reaction mixture to the room
temperature (rt), it was refluxed for ∼4 h (TLC). After evaporation of
the volatile materials, the product mixture was poured into 100 mL of
distilled water, acidified with HCl (1 N) (at -5 °C) until the pH became
acidic, and further extracted with AcOEt (3 × 50 mL). The combined
organic phase was washed and dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate,
followed by removal of the solvent under reduced pressure. The resulting
material was collected, washed several times with light petroleum (40-60
°C), and crystallized from the proper solvent. General Method for the
Preparation of the Bisphosphonates (BPs) 8, 10, 13, and 16. Following the
general procedure, a mixture of 8.4 mmol of amines 6, 9, 11, or 14, 1.24
g of triethyl orthoformate (2) (8.4 mmol), and 2.7 g diethyl
phosphite-sodium salt (16.8 mmol) in 20 mL of dry toluene were allowed to
react under similar experimental conditions. After the usual workup, the
residue was crystallized from the proper solvent to give 8, 10, 13, and
16, respectively.
Tetraethyl[8-(4-fluorophenyl)-3-oxo-6-phenyl-2,3-dihydro-1-H-pyrrolo-[2',3':4,5]-thieno[2,3-b]pyridine-2,2-diyl]bisphosphonate
(16). Orange substance; yield 74%. mp 296-298 °C (MeOH). IR (KBr, cm-1):
νmax 3334 (NH), 1666 (C═O), 1268 (P═O, free), 1230 (P═O, bonded), 1153,
1115 (2P-O-C). 1H NMR [DMSO-d6]: δ 1.27, 1.31 (2dt, JH-H = 7.6, 4JP-H =
4.5 Hz, 2 × 6H, 2POCCH3), 4.24, 4.33 (2qt, 3JP-H = 11.7 Hz, 2 × 4H,
2P-O-CH2), 7.20-8.21 (m, 10H, H-Ar), 10.01 (br s, 1H, HN) ppm. 13C NMR
[DMSO-d6]: δ 179.30 (t, 2JP-C = 16.6 Hz, C═O), 166.24 (C-F), 153.11
(Ph-C-N), 149.22 (N═C-S), 146.21 (t, 3JP-C = 7.2 Hz, C-NH), 144.1, 143.9,
137.9, 135.7, 131.4, 129.5, 124.3, 121.9, 119.3, 118.6, 113.2 (C-Ar),
119.9 (t, 3JP-C = 7.4 Hz, C-C═O) 76.5 (t, 1JP-C = 167.4 Hz, C-P2), 61.9
(t, 2JP-C = 16.1 Hz, 2P-O-CH2), 16.7 (t, 3JP-C = 7.5 Hz, 2POCCH3) ppm.
31P NMR [DMSO-d6]: δP 27.1, 28.8 (2d, 2JP-P = 32 Hz, P-C-P) ppm. EI-MS:
m/z (%):631 (14) [M+ - 1], 613 (36) [[M+ - 1]-18 F], 476 (47), [[M+ -
19]-137 C4H10O3P], 339 (100) [[M+ - 19]-274 C8H20O6P2], 137 (66)
(C4H10O3P), 77 (100). Anal. calcd. for C29H31FN2O7P2S (632.6): C, 55.06;
H, 4.94; F, 3.00; N, 4.43; P, 9.79; S, 5.07. Found: C, 55.10; H, 4.99; F,
3.05; N, 4.40; P, 9.75; S, 5.03%.
