$DATUM (1,3-Dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-ylmethyl)-H-phosphinic acid ethyl ester
32 (Scheme 3).4 To compound 30b (1.5 g, 4 mmol) in 10 mL of 10% ethanol
in dichloromethane was added chlorotrimethylsilane (0.65 g, 1.5 equiv., 6
mmol, 0.75 mL) under N2 and the clear solution was stirred for 16 h at
room temperature. The solvent was removed by vacuo and the resulting oil
was purified by column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/Hexanes 3:7, v/v) to
afford the desired product 32 as a white solid (0.75 g, 73%).
(1,3-Dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-ylmethyl)-H-phosphinic acid ethyl ester
32, Yield (0.75 g, 73%). mp 83-85 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 7.70-7.90
(m, 4H), 7.39 (d, J= 579 Hz, 1H), 4.25 (q, J= 7 Hz, J= 14 Hz, 2H), 4.11
(d, J= 10 Hz, 2H), 1.35 (t, J= 7 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.45 MHz) δ
167.3 (2C), 134.6 (2C), 131.8 (2C), 123.8 (2C), 63.1 (d, JPOC = 6 Hz ),
36.4 (d, JPCN = 100 Hz), 16.5 (d, JPOCC = 6 Hz ); 31P NMR (CDCl3, 121.47
MHz) δ 26.1 (dm, J= 579 Hz); HRMS (EI+) calc for C11H12NO4P 253.0504,
found 253.0496.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of P,N-heterocycles from ω-amino-H-phosphinates:
conformationally restricted α-amino acid analogs
