$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of the Bisphosphonates (BPs)
4a-4g. A mixture of 8.4 mmol of amines 3a-3g and triethyl orthoformate
(2) (8.7 mmol, 1.3 g) in 15 mL of dry toluene was heated under
simultaneous distillation by the use of a Dean-Stark trap. After
completion of the reaction, ∼6 h (TLC), the product mixture was
concentrated under reduced pressure to its half. A solution of (18.0
mmol, 2.5 g) diethyl hydrogen phosphite (1) in 15 mL of dry toluene
containing sodium metal (18.5 mmol, 0.4 g) was added to the produced
residue dropwise at 0 °C. After warming the reaction mixture to the room
temperature (rt), it was refluxed for ∼4 h (TLC). After evaporation of
the volatile materials, the product mixture was poured into 100 mL of
distilled water, acidified with HCl (1 N) (at -5 °C) until the pH became
acidic, and further extracted with AcOEt (3 × 50 mL). The combined
organic phase was washed and dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate,
followed by removal of the solvent under reduced pressure. The resulting
material was collected, washed several times with light petroleum (40-60
°C), and crystallized from the proper solvent to give the corresponding
BPs 4a-4g. Tetraethyl
{[(2,6-dioxo-1,2,3,6-tetrahydropyrimidin-4-yl)amino]methylene}bis-phosphonate
(4e). Yellow material; 73.4%. mp 212-215 °C (EtOH). IR (KBr, cm-1): νmax
3454-3340w (NHs), 1687, 1638 (2C═O), 1255 (P═O, free), 1233 (P═O,
bonded), 1150, 1117 (2P-O-C). 1H NMR [DMSO-d6]: δ = 1.16, 1.25 (2dt, JH-H
= 6.7, 4JP-H = 3.8 Hz, 2 × 6H, 2POC-CH3), 3.91, 4.20 (2qt, 3JP-H = 12.1
Hz, 2 × 4H, 2P-O-CH2), 5.84 (d, 2JP-H = 17.8 Hz, 1H, HC-P2), 6.24 (s, 1H,
H-C-5), 8.67, 10.48, 11.33 (3br, 3 × 1H, 3 NH) ppm. 13C NMR [DMSO-d6]: δ
= 162.7, 155.7 (2C═O), 153.7 (t, 3JP-C = 8.4 Hz, C-4), 82.6 (t, 4JP-C
=4.3 Hz, C-5), 62.6 (t, 2JP-C = 14.3 Hz, 2P-O-CH2), 53.2 (t, 1JP-C =
134.6 Hz, C-P2), 15.5 (t, 3JP-C = 4.8 Hz, Hz, 2POCCH3) ppm. 31P NMR
(DMSO-d6): δP = 23.8, 25.3 (2d, 2JP-P = 29 Hz, P-C-P) ppm. EI-MS: m/z
(%): 412 (9) [M+ - 1], 410 (10) [M+ - 3], 273 (18) [(M+ -
3)-137(C4H10O3P)], 137 (80) (C4H10O3P), 136 (100) [(M+ -
3)-274(C8H20O6P2)], 124 (48) [(M+ - 3)-286(C9H20O6P2)], 112 (78). Anal.
calcd. for C13H25N3O8P2 (413.3): C, 37.78; H, 6.10; N, 10.17; P, 14.99.
Found: C, 37.92; H, 6.17; N, 10.21; P, 14.93%.
