$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure: To the solution of ketone
(2 mmol) in solvent (3 mL, see Table 1), the benzylamine (2 mmol) or
NH4(CO3)2 (6 mmol), anhyd MgSO4 (2 mmol) and Pht-122 (10 mol%; 0.2 mmol)
as a catalyst were added. The reaction mixture was heated for 3-4 h. Then
diethylphosphite (2.4 mmol) was added. The reaction mixture was stirred
for 12- 24 h (see Table 1). The desiccant was then filtered and washed
with 2 mL of CH2Cl2. The solvent was evaporated, and the residue was
purified by chromatography on silica gel (eluent: CH2Cl2/MeOH = 20:1). In
the case of steric hindered and cage ketones (adamantanone-2, camphor and
norbornanone) 50% amine excess is required. Compound (2b)c. Yield 70%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Kabachnick-Fields reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A novel catalytic three-component synthesis (Kabachnik-Fields reaction)
of α-aminophosphonates from ketones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Matveeva, Elena D.; Podrugina, Tatyana A.; Tishkovskaya, Elena V.;
Tomilova, Larisa G.; Zefirov, Nikolay S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2003), (15), 2321-2324

